<h2>7. Expected Economic and Social Impact</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Massive Municipal Budget Savings:</strong> By enforcing contractor warranty liabilities (DLP) and conducting proactive crack sealing prior to Kiremt, RoadEye™ saves an estimated <strong>15 to 30 Million ETB</strong> per year for a medium-sized municipality like Debre Berhan.</li>
    <li><strong>Foreign Currency Preservation:</strong> Eliminates millions of USD in imports of proprietary laser equipment and foreign inspection consultants.</li>
    <li><strong>Saving Human Lives:</strong> Eliminating severe potholes and providing in-cabin collision alerts significantly reduces rollover collisions, sudden lane-swerving crashes, and vehicle damage on Route A2.</li>
    <li><strong>Youth Employment & Tech Innovation:</strong> Generates high-skill technology employment in AI annotation, GIS data analysis, sensor installation, and municipal infrastructure management in Debre Berhan.</li>
    <li><strong>Environmental Sustainability:</strong> Preventive localized patching uses only 5% of the carbon-intensive hot bitumen and aggregate required for full-depth reconstruction.</li>
</ul>

